cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use CheckCardioNet in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "CheckCardioNet: Predicting ICI-driven cardiovascular acceleration risk and individualizing ICI recommendations from a tumor checkpoint expression profile"
abstract: >-
  CheckCardioNet is an open-source command-line prediction tool for cardio-
  oncology. Given a patient's tumor checkpoint expression profile (z-score),
  cancer type, and baseline cardiovascular susceptibility, it computes a
  per-drug CVD-acceleration score and produces an individualized ICI
  recommendation, ranking candidate drugs by net benefit and surfacing
  dual-benefit alternatives where appropriate. Pre-trained Mendelian-
  randomization causal effects, bidirectionality scores, and a dual-benefit
  drug atlas are bundled inside the package — no external data download is
  required.
authors:
  - name: "CheckCardioNet Authors"
keywords:
  - immune-checkpoint
  - cardio-oncology
  - cardiotoxicity
  - drug-recommendation
  - precision-oncology
  - bioinformatics
